Z||000000||ChadMan||03-07-2001||09:10 AM||||Are any of you Fieroholics following the "IT" story?<BR> <A HREF="http://dailynews.yahoo.com/h/ap/20010306/bs/mystery_invention_1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://dailynews.yahoo.com/h/ap/20010306/bs/mystery_invention_1.html</A> <P>I don't care about the scooter, but if Kamen has made a breakthrough with a safe, powerful hydrogen engine, that could mean we will be driving cars forever!  <P>Forget being forced to ride a slow, stinking bus with 40 strangers, or having to drive an electric car that runs out of juice after 50 miles.  Fifty years from now, you could still be able to get in your convenient, fun personal automobile and go anywhere, and the only emissions will be helium and water!<P>Does anybody know any more about hydrogen engines?  I know we have some engineers out there...||||reg||3
Z||000001||deceler8||03-07-2001||09:22 AM||||As far as I know, Kamen has been fooling around with the Stirling engine concept (external combustion) for years and this is probably the engine configuration that "IT" uses.<P>This would indeed be a huge breakthrough as at the present time the energy density of hydrogen as it would now be used in an application such as this is not much better than a lead-acid battery.<P>Kamen also has quite a few third-world applications for the Stirling besides transportation.<P>Another breakthrough is the use of gyroscopes and computers to control motion in the "IT"...it may only have one wheel. We'll just have to see how much trunk space he can design into "IT"...lol.||||reg||1
